ned her PhD in 2021 under Professor Martin Jagersand&#39;s supervision, wor=
king in vision for robotics. Her research was recognized with the KUKA inno=
vation finalist award in 2018 and in the Black in AI Keynote talk at NeurIP=
S 2022.=C2=A0 Her thesis focused on learning video object segmentation with=
 limited labelled data, where she worked on the intersection between video =
object segmentation and few-shot learning with application to both autonomo=
us driving and robot manipulation. As a proud Canadian, she has continuousl=
y contributed to diversity and inclusion efforts, especially within Canada,=
 through founding the Ro&#39;ya Community for Africans in Computer Vision.<=
